---
import ConverterPage from '../components/ConverterPage.astro';
---

<ConverterPage
  path="/marathi-font-converter"
  lede="Planned: a Marathi font converter for Shree Lipi and other legacy Marathi fonts to Unicode."
>
  <h2>Planned, not started</h2>
  <p>
    Marathi is written in Devanagari, the same script as Hindi, so this is the
    closest of the planned scripts to what the site already does. Some of the
    engine, meaning the matra reordering, the reph and the conjunct handling, carries
    over directly.
  </p>
  <p>
    The character maps do not. Shree Lipi and the other Marathi DTP fonts have
    their own key arrangements, and Marathi uses some conjuncts and the eyelash
    <span lang="mr">ऱ</span> in ways Hindi does not. Reusing the Kruti Dev map
    would produce Marathi that is wrong in precisely the places Marathi differs
    from Hindi, which is the hardest kind of error to notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    This will be built only after a keyword check says it is worth doing and a
    mapping has been tested against real Marathi documents. Meanwhile, if your
    document is Hindi in Kruti Dev, <a href="/">the main converter</a> handles it.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
